# Sanitized UFW baseline
# Project: VPS Cloud Infrastructure Lab
# Phase: Phase 1 - VPS Baseline & Security Hardening
#
# This file documents the intended baseline firewall posture.
# It is not an exported production firewall config.

Default incoming policy: deny
Default outgoing policy: allow

Allowed inbound traffic:

| Rule | Purpose |
|---|---|
| OpenSSH | Administrative SSH access |
| 80/tcp | HTTP traffic and certificate validation |
| 443/tcp | HTTPS public services |

Expected public exposure:

| Port | Purpose |
|---|---|
| SSH | Server administration |
| HTTP | Web traffic and certificate validation |
| HTTPS | Secure public services |

Do not directly expose:

- Application ports such as 3000, 5000, 8000, or 8080
- Database ports such as 5432, 3306, or 6379
- Portainer
- Monitoring dashboards
- Internal APIs
- Admin-only services

Validation command:

    sudo ufw status verbose

Design note:

Public services should eventually be routed through a reverse proxy with HTTPS.
Admin services should stay private through Tailscale whenever possible.
